## Epic 4: Handle exceptions and monitor performance

### US-09: Understand why I was declined
**As a** declined applicant, **I want** a clear explanation and next steps, **so that** I know what I can do next.
**Requirement:** FR-13 | **Priority:** Should | **Points:** 3

**Acceptance criteria**
- **Given** my application is declined, **when** I am notified, **then** the message explains the reason in plain language without revealing fraud-detection rules.
- **Given** I receive a decline message, **when** I read it, **then** it includes how to contact support or visit a branch.

### US-10: Track onboarding funnel performance
**As a** Head of Retail Banking, **I want** a dashboard of the onboarding funnel, **so that** I can see where customers drop off and measure improvement.
**Requirement:** FR-15 | **Priority:** Should | **Points:** 8

**Acceptance criteria**
- **Given** I open the dashboard, **when** it loads, **then** I see applications started, completed, abandoned, referred and declined for a selected period.
- **Given** I select a step in the funnel, **when** I drill down, **then** I see the drop-off rate for that step.
- **Given** data refreshes, **when** a new day starts, **then** the dashboard shows data up to the end of the previous day.

### US-11: Assist a customer in branch (Could have)
**As a** branch consultant, **I want to** start a digital application on behalf of a customer, **so that** customers without smartphones can still use the new process.
**Requirement:** FR-14 | **Priority:** Could | **Points:** 8

**Acceptance criteria**
- **Given** I am logged in as a consultant, **when** I start an application, **then** the customer completes verification on the branch tablet.
- **Given** a consultant-assisted application, **when** it is saved, **then** it records the consultant ID for audit purposes.

